.TH ANCHORAGE 1 "November 2026" "Anchorage 0.9.0~beta1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anchorage \- manage drives, network shares and /etc/fstab on KDE Plasma
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anchorage
[\fIQt and KDE options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Anchorage
shows the drives, folders shown in a second place (bind mounts) and SMB and
NFS network shares that this computer knows about, and lets you mount them,
unmount them and change how they are mounted. It edits
.I /etc/fstab
for you, explains each option in plain words, checks every change before saving
it and keeps a backup of the file before each change.
.PP
Anchorage itself never runs as root. Changes to system files are made by
.IR anchorage-helper ,
which polkit starts as root after asking for a password.
Members of the
.B driveadmins
group may make every change with their own password; members of
.B netmount
may add network shares and save logins for them. The package creates both
groups but adds nobody to them; to give someone access, run for example
.PP
.RS
sudo adduser alice netmount
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/fstab
The file Anchorage edits.
.TP
.I /etc/anchorage/backups/
A copy of /etc/fstab from before each change.
.TP
.I /etc/anchorage/credentials/
Saved logins for SMB shares, readable only by root.
.TP
.I /etc/anchorage/config
Settings made in Anchorage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES
Set to
.B anchorage.*.info=true
to log what Anchorage does, for a bug report. Beta versions log this by
default. Passwords are never logged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fstab (5),
.BR mount (8),
.BR mount.cifs (8),
.BR nfs (5)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/oarko/Anchorage/issues
